%description:

Tcp.sendDataWithFirstAck:on -- data that waits during the handshake goes with the ACK of the SYN-ACK.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "an active open sends data that waits at the end of the handshake with
the ACK of the SYN-ACK".

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false). The code: the end of an active open sends
the data that waits with the ACK of the SYN-ACK, or a bare ACK first
(TcpAlgorithmBase::established()). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, which sends 1000 bytes in the same instant as its open. Observation:
level 1, the first segment of host1 after the SYN carries data.

%# parameter: Tcp.sendDataWithFirstAck
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.sendDataWithFirstAck
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSendDataWithFirstAckOn")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
            app.sendData(app.socket(), 1000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertPacket("pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .describe("the first segment of host1 after the SYN, with data")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSendDataWithFirstAckOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.sendDataWithFirstAck = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSendDataWithFirstAckOn: PASS
